# Task 8 — Project Archiving

Projects should **never be permanently deleted**.

### 8.1 Archive Project

* Replace permanent project deletion with **Archive Project**.
* Preserve all project data.
* Remove archived projects from normal project selectors/views.

### 8.2 Archive Section

Create:

```text
Settings
└── Archives
    ├── Archived Projects
    └── ...
```

Allow authorized users to:

* View archived projects.
* Inspect project data.
* Restore projects where permitted.

Maintain project history and relationships after archiving.

---

# Task 9 — Saved Views & Reusable Filters

Add reusable saved views throughout the application.

Users should be able to:

* Apply filters.
* Configure sorting.
* Configure visible columns where applicable.
* Save the configuration.
* Name the saved view.
* Reopen it later.
* Update/delete saved views.

Example:

```text
My Views
├── High Priority Tasks
├── Current Sprint
├── Unassigned Tasks
└── Overdue Tasks
```

Saved views should respect the user's project permissions.

---

# Task 10 — Project Duplication

Allow authorized users to duplicate existing projects.

Useful for:

* Recurring projects.
* Similar projects.
* Standard project templates.
* Repeated task structures.
* Repeated sprint structures.

### Duplication Options

Allow users to choose what should be copied:

* Project information.
* Tasks.
* Task structure.
* Sprints.
* Milestones.
* Workflows.
* Custom fields.
* Other reusable configuration.

Do not blindly copy users/resources unless explicitly selected.

---

# Task 11 — Methodology-Specific Project Experience

Support different project methodologies.

Examples:

```text
Project
├── Kanban
├── Waterfall
├── ...
```

The project methodology should be selected during project creation/configuration.

### Kanban Project

When a Kanban project is selected:

* Show Kanban board.
* Show Kanban-specific metrics.
* Show relevant dashboard.
* Show workflow-oriented information.
* Hide irrelevant methodology-specific components.

### Waterfall Project

When a Waterfall project is selected:

* Show Waterfall-specific dashboard.
* Show phases.
* Show milestones.
* Show timeline/dependencies.
* Show relevant project information.

### Dynamic Project Experience

```text
Select Project
      ↓
Read Project Methodology
      ↓
Load Methodology Configuration
      ↓
Display Relevant Dashboard
      ↓
Display Relevant Views
```

The architecture should make it easy to add additional methodologies later.

---

# Task 12 — UI Components & Library Refactor

Audit the existing UI before implementing new dashboards.

### 12.1 Component Audit

Identify components that are currently:

* Hardcoded.
* Custom-built unnecessarily.
* Duplicating existing functionality.
* Implementing charts manually.
* Implementing tables manually.
* Implementing icons manually.
* Implementing animations manually.
* Implementing complex UI interactions that can be handled by established libraries.

Create an inventory:

| Component  | Current Implementation | Problem                | Suggested Library  | Refactor Priority |
| ---------- | ---------------------- | ---------------------- | ------------------ | ----------------- |
| Charts     | Custom                 | Maintenance            | Chart library      | High              |
| Tables     | Custom                 | Missing features       | Data-table library | High              |
| Icons      | Custom                 | Large maintenance cost | Icon library       | Medium            |
| Calendar   | Custom                 | Complex interactions   | Calendar library   | High              |
| Kanban     | Custom                 | Interaction complexity | DnD/Kanban library | High              |
| Animations | Custom                 | Inconsistent           | Animation library  | Medium            |

### 12.2 Library Selection

For every identified component:

* Research established libraries.
* Prefer actively maintained libraries.
* Prefer libraries compatible with the existing Next.js/React stack.
* Avoid rebuilding functionality already solved by mature libraries.
* Document the selected library and reason for adoption.

### 12.3 Refactor

After the audit:

* Refactor high-impact components first.
* Replace unnecessary custom implementations.
* Preserve existing behavior.
* Add/update tests where required.
* Avoid introducing unnecessary dependencies.

